gn with Death. Persephone is in the Underworld only one season of the year, maybe two; she's in the land of the living for at least two others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:46:49-07:00","id":884188,"title":"","content":"Harvesters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:32:04-07:00","id":884227,"title":"","content":"that would be a decent nickname for a so for a Sophros, though so would reaper, planter, and gardener.<br /> <br /> someone suggested Elysium as a possible supernal realm for another path. I think it might work well for this path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-07-2016, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T00:50:05-07:00","id":884445,"title":"","content":"I think of Mediums as the bridge between the living and the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T01:01:26-07:00","id":884449,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T01:41:48-07:00","id":884468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=884227#post884227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that would be a decent nickname for a so for a Sophros, though so would reaper, planter, and gardener.<br /> <br /> someone suggested Elysium as a possible supernal realm for another path. I think it might work well for this path.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Definitely, it evokes the Eleusinian Mysteries. (Ok, yes, I know the name actually comes from Eleusis, but it still fits and the words are related)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T04:51:03-07:00","id":884548,"title":"","content":"Oxlahun the Maya equivalent of Olympus looks like a pyramid fused with a giant tree. It could work well for the Path imagery.<br /> <br /> Ok I'm biaised because when I see a Life/Death Path I think of South America. (It's my headcanon the Sophroi Aeon are Xipe Totec and Santa Muerte though) Mesoamericans did an interesting symbolic link between bones and seed and the whole &quot;spill blood to feed the universe&quot; is great praxis for Life/Death<br /> <br /> For the Supernal inhabitants Serpents would be the best fit. Ents have zero Death symbolism while Serpent is a pretty common symbol for the cycle of Life and Death. Also it's a mythic rule everywhere there are mystic trees there are serpentine guardians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2225,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","user":"ganonso","date":". 05-07-2016, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T07:31:00-07:00","id":884607,"title":"","content":"Might Oxlahun work better as an Emanation, as with Yggdrasil? <br /> <br /> OK; Serpents it is. For now, there are Serpents in Elysium. <br /> <br /> And to the extent that there's <i>any</i> \u201ccanon\u201d associated with a purely fandom product, consider your Sophroi Aeons canonized. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> (I figure that when <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> comes out, I'll update this further, paralleling the expanded Supernal Realms from there.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T08:39:32-07:00","id":884647,"title":"","content":"Still need a replacement Realm for Mount Qaf, something that works better as an environment (what Maestros Mage Sight sees) than as a place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:00:22-07:00","id":884932,"title":"","content":"Egyptian called the desert around their home Deshret the place of desolation whence ennemies came from. It was the land of chaos so maybe nice for a Forces/Spirit. I think the lack of Prime would translate in Mage's imagery as a wasteland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:05:16-07:00","id":884935,"title":"","content":"Well Qaf as a concept is supposed to be a Mountain and somehow surround the world, so I actually do think it works as the Supernal Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:34:24-07:00","id":884951,"title":"","content":"Speaking more generally, maybe a focus on accession, high places, and the sky?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:44:51-07:00","id":884963,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u201cThe Realm is one of raging elemental forces, but not in the sense of the raw power of the Aether \u2014 the Sixth Realm is made of flame, lightning, freezing cold, and crashing sound, but they move with purpose, filled with alien intelligence that can be contacted and \u2014 for those that learn the Path well \u2014 coerced into doing the new mage's bidding. The inhabitants are beings made out of the same purposeful energy, creatures of smokeless flame that the Pentacle orders, at least, are calling <i>Djinn</i>.\u201d</span><br /> \u2014 <b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b>, p.100","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:37:46-07:00","id":884999,"title":"","content":"Actually you know what.Raging elements who can be bargained with. That totally in the range of Inuit myth and esthetic. One advantage would be to avoid the correlation with the Aether with two Fire Realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:57:04-07:00","id":885042,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u201cThough Middle Eastern symbolism is obviously the orders' starting point for experimentation, mages seek other elements of Sleeper culture and occult practice that might have power.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> OK; do the Inuit have something that could be used as a Realm name? Preferably something that wouldn't clash <i>too</i> horribly with calling the denizens \u201cdjinn\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T21:17:41-07:00","id":885143,"title":"","content":"I am <i>definitely </i>liking these alternative Paths. Maybe enough to incorporate them into my stuff so that I can feature a setup like the Ravnica Guilds for <i>ten</i> Paths.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, though, framing these Paths in the settings of Dark Eras might be somewhat difficult. Or, at least, require a lot of work. This might especially be the case for the Sundered World and To The Strongest, though for the latter I can see these Paths being alternative iterations of the Fivefold Soul (Acanthus and Anakalos being Ren, Mastigos and Kleos for Ba, etc.).<br /> <br /> Also, may I ask where you derived the names for these Paths? We know, for certain, that the present day names for the canon Paths originated from Greece, so I was curious which Greek words you used for this set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T22:19:49-07:00","id":885164,"title":"","content":"For most of them, I started with the \u201cPath of\u2026\u201d names: Discovery, Excellence, Mastery, and Balance, then mangled them to end with \u201c-os\u201d. I originally did the same with Enlightenment, which gave me Diafos; but then <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"801\" data-vbnamecard=\"801\">Grytorm</a> suggested Kleos, which apparently means \u201cto hear\u201d but has connotations of tales of glory. <br /> <br /> I'm not seeing the difficulty of integrating these into the Dark Eras; at least, it's no more trouble than integrating the official five Paths into the Dark Eras. <br /> <br /> It's worth noting that while an effort has been made in 2e to treat each of the five official Paths as equally reliant on both Ruling Arcana, there's still a bit of a bias toward the Subtle Arcana. When using all ten Paths, one option would be to play up this bias: call them the Subtle Paths or the Recondite Paths or the Paths of the Soul, or similar terms, and think of them being slightly lopsided: the Acanthus Rule Fate <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Time</span>; the Mastigos Rule Mind <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Space</span>; the Moros (\u201cPath of Doom!\u201d) Rule Death <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Matter</span>; the Obrimos Rule Prime <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Forces</span>; and the Thyrsus Rule Spirit <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Life</span>. There are no mechanical consequences for this, any more than there are any systemic distinctions between Subtle and Gross Arcana; it's purely a matter of one's mindset. <br /> <br /> But if you go with that mindset, then these \u201cother five Paths\u201d become \u201cthe Gross Paths\u201d, \u201cthe Manifest Paths\u201d, or \u201cthe Paths of the World\u201d, with an equally slight bias toward their Gross Ruling Arcana: the Anakalos Rule Space <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Fate</span>; the Aretos Rule Matter <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Prime</span>; the Kleos Rule Time <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Mind</span>; the M\u00e6stros Rule Forces <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Spirit</span>; and the Sophros Rule Life <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Death</span>. <br /> <br /> In <i>To the Strongest</i>, the Egyptian magi would latch on to the correlations between the Paths of the Soul and the Egyptian five-fold soul, whereas the Indo-greek magi might latch onto correlations between the Paths of the World and their notion of Elementalism (with the Elemental Mastery Legacies being based off of these new Paths rather than the original five). Each would have a mystery of five Paths that don't fit their model, and the two views would be complementary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-08-2016, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T00:16:11-07:00","id":885226,"title":"","content":"I've updated the first post to include a \u201cHow to use these Paths\u201d section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T01:02:21-07:00","id":885248,"title":"","content":"Inuits places names and concepts courtesy of the supplement for the Inue by John Scion ressources<br /> Udlormiut: Godrealm<br /> Adlivun: Watery Underworld<br /> Ukiuk: Frost<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T08:32:14-07:00","id":885393,"title":"","content":"So for moving the elemental associations, the Anakalos would be Air, Areatos Earth (Tamers of Stone being architects fits well), Kleos the Akasha (it''s literally their Realm!), Maestros Flame, and Sophos Water?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-08-2016, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:09:50-07:00","id":885414,"title":"","content":"I don't have my copy of Legacies: the Ancient to check it; but from what I remember of them, that sounds about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:49:49-07:00","id":885440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=885164#post885164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For most of them, I started with the \u201cPath of\u2026\u201d names: Discovery, Excellence, Mastery, and Balance, then mangled them to end with \u201c-os\u201d. I originally did the same with Enlightenment, which gave me Diafos; but then <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"801\" data-vbnamecard=\"801\">Grytorm</a> suggested Kleos, which apparently means \u201cto hear\u201d but has connotations of tales of glory.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing the difficulty of integrating these into the Dark Eras; at least, it's no more trouble than integrating the official five Paths into the Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that while an effort has been made in 2e to treat each of the five official Paths as equally reliant on both Ruling Arcana, there's still a bit of a bias toward the Subtle Arcana. When using all ten Paths, one option would be to play up this bias: call them the Subtle Paths or the Recondite Paths or the Paths of the Soul, or similar terms, and think of them being slightly lopsided: the Acanthus Rule Fate <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Time</span>; the Mastigos Rule Mind <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Space</span>; the Moros (\u201cPath of Doom!\u201d) Rule Death <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Matter</span>; the Obrimos Rule Prime <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Forces</span>; and the Thyrsus Rule Spirit <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Life</span>. There are no mechanical consequences for this, any more than there are any systemic distinctions between Subtle and Gross Arcana; it's purely a matter of one's mindset.<br /> <br /> But if you go with that mindset, then these \u201cother five Paths\u201d become \u201cthe Gross Paths\u201d, \u201cthe Manifest Paths\u201d, or \u201cthe Paths of the World\u201d, with an equally slight bias toward their Gross Ruling Arcana: the Anakalos Rule Space <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Fate</span>; the Aretos Rule Matter <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Prime</span>; the Kleos Rule Time <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Mind</span>; the M\u00e6stros Rule Forces <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Spirit</span>; and the Sophros Rule Life <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Death</span>.<br /> <br /> In <i>To the Strongest</i>, the Egyptian magi would latch on to the correlations between the Paths of the Soul and the Egyptian five-fold soul, whereas the Indo-greek magi might latch onto correlations between the Paths of the World and their notion of Elementalism (with the Elemental Mastery Legacies being based off of these new Paths rather than the original five). Each would have a mystery of five Paths that don't fit their model, and the two views would be complementary.</div> </div> </div> </div>These notes are definitely worth pondering over. Having the two sets be strongly associated with one of two cultural traditions would certainly add to the Mystery that Mages in Egypt, Greece, and India could deal with in their attempts to reconcile their respective beliefs with &quot;foreign magic&quot;. On the other hand, there's nothing wrong with mixing and matching the sets together. The Weret-Hekau might place more distinction on the Subtle Arcana (regardless of whether one's Path was of the Soul or of the World), while the Greek and Indian cults identified more with the powers of the Gross Arcana (again, regardless of Path).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T18:19:53-07:00","id":888725,"title":"","content":"I've been rethinking the Anakalos, and I think I got their focus wrong. Consider: the purviews of Fate are blessings, hexes, probability, fortune, oaths, promises, intentions, and destiny; the purviews of Space are distance, separation, sympathy, conjuration, scrying, and warding. What's the greatest synergy between these? It's not distance or separation, as implied by my original focus on explorers \u2014 although there is something to that, which should not get lost (no pun intended). No, the greatest synergy is between Sympathy, oaths, promises, and intentions. The core of the synergy is that all of these deal with what's important to the subject. Consider this paragraph, extracted from Space's discussion about Sympathy: <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u201cSympathetic links manipulated with the Space Arcanum echo from the Supernal to the Fallen, wreaking subtle but long-standing changes in the subjects. Sever a man's link to his husband and the relationship cools and grows distant. Create a bond between a woman and a gun, and she'll find herself thinking about it, dreaming about it \u2014 and left to their own devices odds are good woman and gun will cross paths.\u201d</span></div><br /> That is, you have Sympathetic connections to that which you care about, and vice versa. This sense of importance resonates nicely with Fate's purview of intentions, which is <i>also</i> about what's important to you: you generally don't make promises or swear oaths about things that don't matter to you. With this in mind, the mages on this Path aren't explorers so much as they're <i>deal-makers</i>: diplomats and merchants. At its most noble, this Path is about meeting peoples' needs and fulfilling their desires; at its worst, it's about the con artist and the politician who exploit peoples' needs and twist their desires to their own ends. It's not a Path of Discovery (beyond the extent that <i>any</i> mage can be said to be on a Path of Discovery, given their addiction to Mysteries); it's a Path of <i>Value</i>, or perhaps of Meaning. To the extent that other purviews factor in, distance and separation are important to the traveling merchant, while scrying keeps lines of communication open between a foreign dignitary and her homeland; while blessings and hexes give supernatural weight to deals that are made, fortune and destiny let you seek out opportunities, and probability helps with \u201cthere is no reward without risk\u201d. Speaking of which:<br /> <br /> Risk and Reward still works as the central dichotomy of the Path; in fact, it works even better than it used to under the exploration theme. But the stereotypes and imagery need an overhaul; and even the Path's <i>name</i> might need to be rethought. Maybe the Axios? (Ax\u00eda is greek for \u201cvalue, worth, merit, valuation, denomination, worthiness\u201d). <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:50:55-07:00","id":888832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=888725#post888725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been rethinking the Anakalos, and I think I got their focus wrong. Consider: the purviews of Fate are blessings, hexes, probability, fortune, oaths, promises, intentions, and destiny; the purviews of Space are distance, separation, sympathy, conjuration, scrying, and warding. What's the greatest synergy between these? It's not distance or separation, as implied by my original focus on explorers \u2014 although there is something to that, which should not get lost (no pun intended). No, the greatest synergy is between Sympathy, oaths, promises, and intentions. The core of the synergy is that all of these deal with what's important to the subject. Consider this paragraph, extracted from Space's discussion about Sympathy:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u201cSympathetic links manipulated with the Space Arcanum echo from the Supernal to the Fallen, wreaking subtle but long-standing changes in the subjects. Sever a man's link to his husband and the relationship cools and grows distant. Create a bond between a woman and a gun, and she'll find herself thinking about it, dreaming about it \u2014 and left to their own devices odds are good woman and gun will cross paths.\u201d</span></div><br /> That is, you have Sympathetic connections to that which you care about, and vice versa. This sense of importance resonates nicely with Fate's purview of intentions, which is <i>also</i> about what's important to you: you generally don't make promises or swear oaths about things that don't matter to you. With this in mind, the mages on this Path aren't explorers so much as they're <i>deal-makers</i>: diplomats and merchants. At its most noble, this Path is about meeting peoples' needs and fulfilling their desires; at its worst, it's about the con artist and the politician who exploit peoples' needs and twist their desires to their own ends. It's not a Path of Discovery (beyond the extent that <i>any</i> mage can be said to be on a Path of Discovery, given their addiction to Mysteries); it's a Path of <i>Value</i>, or perhaps of Meaning. To the extent that other purviews factor in, distance and separation are important to the traveling merchant, while scrying keeps lines of communication open between a foreign dignitary and her homeland; while blessings and hexes give supernatural weight to deals that are made, fortune and destiny let you seek out opportunities, and probability helps with \u201cthere is no reward without risk\u201d. Speaking of which:<br /> <br /> Risk and Reward still works as the central dichotomy of the Path; in fact, it works even better than it used to under the exploration theme. But the stereotypes and imagery need an overhaul; and even the Path's <i>name</i> might need to be rethought. Maybe the Axios? (Ax\u00eda is greek for \u201cvalue, worth, merit, valuation, denomination, worthiness\u201d).<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am <i>definitely</i> liking these changes. I think it makes more sense to refer to the Axios as &quot;the Path of Meaning&quot;, especially since its two Ruling Arcana defines the meaning of one's life through his destiny, intentions, and promises (w/ Fate) and his ties with the persons, places, and things around him (w/ Space). Discovery for Mages who Awaken to the Firmament is about realizing who you are, and how you must overcome trials and tribulations in your life in order to find the answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T11:44:31-07:00","id":916928,"title":"","content":"OK; I've got skeletal write-ups set up for each Path; please review the relevant posts on the first page. Let me emphasize that these are <i>skeletal</i>: I have the framework set up, but I have almost no meat on the bones. I'm seeking input; this is a really big task for one person to do solo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T19:25:36-07:00","id":917101,"title":"","content":"I'd remove the whole story bit of the Time Mind mages simply because Fate is THE story arcanum. Otherwise these are very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T14:28:58-07:00","id":918251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=917101#post917101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd remove the whole story bit of the Time Mind mages simply because Fate is THE story arcanum. Otherwise these are very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stories that the Kleos deal with aren't about narrative structure; they're about oral history. They're grounded in events that actually happened. And given the abilities of the Time Arcanum, a Bard has the potential to not only recount history, but to literally revise it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T15:37:13-07:00","id":918276,"title":"","content":"Hmm...in that case I would try to make it more clear that you're talking about history and not stories. The word story conjures the image of fiction, whereas you're talking about in game nonfiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:22:32-07:00","id":918294,"title":"","content":"I'm open to suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T18:51:07-07:00","id":939262,"title":"","content":"I'm looking for advice on what each Paths tarot associations should be. In my first iteration, the alchemists had Temperance, the astrologers had the Star, the druids had the Wheel of Fortune, the sages had the Magician, and the sorcerers had the Emperor. However, that's one each; Even if these choices hold true (which I doubt), I still need a second for each Path. <br /> <br /> There are 22 Major Arcana; the original five Paths have claimed eleven of them:<br /> \u2022 <i>Acanthus:</i> the Fool, the Wheel of Fortune.<br /> \u2022 <i>Mastigos:</i> the Devil, Temperance. <br /> \u2022 <i>Moros:</i> Death, the World. <br /> \u2022 <i>Obrimos:</i> Strength, the High Priestess, the Heirophant.<br /> \u2022 <i>Thyrsus:</i> the Hermit, the Moon.<br /> <br /> That leaves us with: <br /> \u2022 the Magician \u2014 power, skill, concentration, action, resourcefulness. Aretos?<br /> \u2022 the Empress \u2014 fertility, femininity, beauty, nature, abundance. Sophros?<br /> \u2022 the Emperor \u2014 authority, father figure, structure, foundation. M\u00e6stros? <br /> \u2022 the Lovers \u2014 love, union, relationships, values alignment, choices. Axios?<br /> \u2022 the Chariot \u2014 control, willpower, victory, assertion, determination. M\u00e6stros?<br /> \u2022 Justice \u2014 justice, fairness, truth, cause and effect, law. Kleos? <br /> \u2022 the Hanged Man \u2014 suspension, restriction, letting go, sacrifice. Axios? <br /> \u2022 the Tower \u2014 disaster, upheaval, sudden change, revelation. The Abyss? <br /> \u2022 the Star \u2014 hope, spirituality, renewal, inspiration, serenity. Kleos?<br /> \u2022 the Sun \u2014 fun, warmth, success, positivity, vitality. Aretos?<br /> \u2022 Judgment \u2014 judgment, rebirth, inner calling, absolution. Sophros?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-28-2016, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:00:46-07:00","id":939268,"title":"","content":"I'll consult my books to see if there any other interesting interpretation that could fit other than what you listed.<br /> For Abyss, I don't think it should have it's own Tarot Card; abyssal &quot;interpretations&quot; of reality could be represented by reversed cards instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T00:06:17-07:00","id":939385,"title":"","content":"Other Path elements that need to be covered: <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><u>Materials</u><br /> Each Path has specific materials that elevate a Magical Tool from merely an object to something resonant with a Supernal Realm, as well as weapons that can replace the traditional knife. <br /> \u2022 <i>Acanthus:</i> Glass, crystal, silver, reflective materials; Rapier, bow, precision weapons <br /> \u2022 <i>Mastigos:</i> Iron, brass, leather, worked materials; Curved sword, whip, cruel weapons <br /> \u2022 <i>Moros:</i> Lead, bone, gems, buried materials; Hammer, mace, crushing weapons <br /> \u2022 <i>Obrimos:</i> Steel, petrified wood, gold, perfected materials; Double-edged sword, spear, noble weapons <br /> \u2022 <i>Thyrsus:</i> Wood, copper, stone, natural materials; Axe, sling, hunting weapons </div>I'm thinking that some overlap might be appropriate here: e.g., the Sophros really ought to have an affinity with wood, and the Aretos should feature perfected materials.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Aretos:</i> copper, mercury, sulfur, purified materials<br /> \u2022 <i>Axios:</i> gold, silver, gemstones, valuable materials; daggers, batons, concealable weapons? <br /> \u2022 <i>Kleos:</i> glass, crystal, transparent materials?; whips, nunchuks, flexible weapons? <br /> \u2022 <i>M\u00e6stros:</i> brass, pewter, alloyed metals; scimitar? <br /> \u2022 <i>Sophros:</i> wood, bone, natural materials; sickle, staff, repurposed weapons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-29-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:59:34-07:00","id":939535,"title":"","content":"With the rethinking of the Axios, their former astrology-oriented imagery doesn't work so well anymore. Hermium Mirror? Great for looking at the Firmament to examine the Stars. But merchants and diplomats don't have any special connection to any of that. So I need a new Watchtower, a new Realm, and a new type of Supernal Entity for the Bargainers. <br /> <br /> While I'm at it, I'm examining some of the other Paths' imagery. The Kleos, for instance: the Tin Flute is all well and good; but 2e has opened up a possibility that wasn't available when I first devised these Paths back in the 1e days: namely, there isn't a Watchtower of the Stone Book anymore. With the Thyrsus shifted over to the Singing Stone, the record-keeping sages can now have a Book- or Scroll-based Watchtower. So, for reference:<br /> <br /> <i>Aretos:</i> was Copper Mallet; still works, though I wouldn't mind something Hermium-based. <br /> <i>Axios:</i> was Hermium Mirror. No clue what it is now. <br /> <i>Kleos:</i> was Tin Flute. Possibly something Bookish. <br /> <i>M\u00e6stros:</i> Brass and Flame. Non-negotiable. <br /> <i>Sophros:</i> Wooden Cup. No reason to change this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T13:53:06-07:00","id":939766,"title":"","content":"BTW, I still really like the astrologers, and I intend to republish them separately, eventually \u2014 which is another reason I don't want to use their imagery for the Axios. They just don't fit <i>this</i> project, as the appropriate Ruling Arcana for them are Time and Space. So they're either a standalone Path or they're part of an exotic set of Paths that aren't constrained to the Ruling pair being one Subtle and one Gross.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:52:34-07:00","id":940694,"title":"","content":"I'm usually not a fan of homebrew material, but this is a very interesting project you have here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I like the methodical approach in covering all aspects a Path needs. Big fan of the Druids in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:15:01-07:00","id":941361,"title":"","content":"I got bored and made some sigils for each Path, if you're interested. There's 5 and the limit for images per post is four, so I'll link to them directly.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/1LTBm28.png\" target=\"_blank\">Aretos</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/f0qgn28.png\" target=\"_blank\">Axios</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/dycn790.png\" target=\"_blank\">Kleos</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/epLsOQl.png\" target=\"_blank\">M\u00e6stros</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/jkrDmP1.png\" target=\"_blank\">Sophros</a></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T20:06:39-07:00","id":941630,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, I can't seem to get the forums' img tag to resize the images. Could you please post smaller versions for me to include in the Path posts? Half the size should do it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T21:01:09-07:00","id":941660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=941630#post941630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, I can't seem to get the forums' img tag to resize the images. Could you please post smaller versions for me to include in the Path posts? Half the size should do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here you go:<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/1ok6iCZ.png\" target=\"_blank\">Aretos</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/7FcJ3YN.png\" target=\"_blank\">Axios</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/mbeMviw.png\" target=\"_blank\">Kleos</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/ml4c2nK.png\" target=\"_blank\">M\u00e6stros</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/KPrWxVz.png\" target=\"_blank\">Sophros</a></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:45:02-07:00","id":950099,"title":"","content":"Perfected Materials: <br /> <br /> <i>Aretos:</i> Hermium<br /> <i>Axios:</i> Adamant<br /> <i>Kleos:</i> Kassiterum<br /> <i>M\u00e6stros:</i> Brontium (when you Perfect Brass, the Zinc gets purged and you get Perfected Copper)<br /> <i>Sophros:</i> Wood<br /> <br /> Note that this changes some of the Watchtowers. Hermium itself isn't a suitable construction material; but as an amalgam with Orichalcum and/or Lunargent (e.g., Thaumium)? That has possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:49:39-07:00","id":950101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=950099#post950099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hermium itself isn't a suitable construction material</div> </div> </div> </div>Constructing the walls of the watchtower from an infinite waterfall of Hermium isn't good enough for you?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:25:10-07:00","id":950252,"title":"","content":"Cute. But the Aretoi are <i>builders</i>, <i>makers</i>. Their focus would be on the fountain or the dam, not the fluid <i>within</i> the fountain or dam. (The Hermium Mirror worked for the astrology-inspired Path because it was described as a rotating disk filled with Hermium, with the rotation causing it to take on a parabolic shape \u2014 a lens-like mirror, useful for stargazing.)<br /> <br /> (The Aretoi are also alchemists; and mercury \u2014 and thus Hermium \u2014 is the most alchemically appropriate of the metals. Medieval alchemists considered liquid mercury to be the <i>essence</i> of metal, separated from any earthen contaminates the give the other metals their solidity.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-13-2016, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T16:33:09-07:00","id":950302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=950252#post950252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cute. But the Aretoi are <i>builders</i>, <i>makers</i>. Their focus would be on the fountain or the dam, not the fluid <i>within</i> the fountain or dam. (The Hermium Mirror worked for the astrology-inspired Path because it was described as a rotating disk filled with Hermium, with the rotation causing it to take on a parabolic shape \u2014 a lens-like mirror, useful for stargazing.)<br /> <br /> (The Aretoi are also alchemists; and mercury \u2014 and thus Hermium \u2014 is the most alchemically appropriate of the metals. Medieval alchemists considered liquid mercury to be the <i>essence</i> of metal, separated from any earthen contaminates the give the other metals their solidity.)</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Aretoi, maybe go for something with glass? Perfected Glass is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T16:47:01-07:00","id":950309,"title":"","content":"It's called \u201cAdamant\u201d, and I assigned it to the Axios Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T01:51:40-08:00","id":1035982,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> As I said I have started to look at the New Paths and I would like to propose this for the Sophros. I started with them as that is where my interests are.<br /> <br /> <b>Sophros: Druids</b> and <b>Blighters </b>on the Path to Elysium, Supernal Realm of Growth and Blight, and abode of Mystical Beasts.<br /> <br /> I am working on flavor text but since this is a slight mechanical change i though that I would broach the subject with you first. I also thought that their Symbols and Myths would follow Opham, It comes complete with its own alphabet and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-22-2017, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T03:19:15-08:00","id":1036001,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind what Death covers. This Path isn't just about physical growth and blight, both of which are covered by Life once you consider the damaging Practices; it's also about the birth, growth, decay, death, and afterlife of the human soul. In this regard, it's kind of like the Thyrsus; but the Subtle aspect is focused in humans rather than animism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T04:09:57-08:00","id":1036015,"title":"","content":"Have you picked an alternative for Mount Qaf yet? If not, how about going with the Smokeless Fire? Metaphysically, a force (fire) that doesn't consume its fuel (smokeless), and doesn't lead to another reaction (prime being inferior), and thus persists in its fury eternally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T04:41:34-08:00","id":1036022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1036001#post1036001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind what Death covers. This Path isn't just about physical growth and blight, both of which are covered by Life once you consider the damaging Practices; it's also about the birth, growth, decay, death, and afterlife of the human soul. In this regard, it's kind of like the Thyrsus; but the Subtle aspect is focused in humans rather than animism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am looking at Blight as Death, but that is why I mentioned it. Going with the Druid Theme I wonder about death at all, Druids deal with Life and Spirit specifically the Nature Spirits and also Death.<br /> <br /> Life and death is a part of the natural things of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:13:02-08:00","id":1036176,"title":"","content":"Wait, so did the Phenomenal World just exist for so long that it's getting reflected in the Supernal and the Lie is breaking down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:20:55-08:00","id":1036182,"title":"","content":"First of i want to say that i really love the extra 5 path concept. <br /> I really liked MtAw except that none of the path presented in the book really spoke to me. And now especially with the Kleos its like i've found something that i didnt realize i felt was missing from the book. So thanks for that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, for the Kleos something that came to me while reading would be the importance of any kind of writing apparatus for symbolic objects for the path.<br /> My guess is that writing itself could be considered a nearly magical discovery and would be extremely important to the path.<br /> After all writing is the way that even unawakened sleeper can use to both transcend Time and Mind.<br /> <br /> Anyway yet again very good ideas and i'll definetively implement them if i ever run a mage game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:55:48-08:00","id":1036260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1036176#post1036176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, so did the Phenomenal World just exist for so long that it's getting reflected in the Supernal and the Lie is breaking down?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, man. Does the chicken come before the egg?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T02:11:50-08:00","id":1036500,"title":"","content":"Here is some of the opening flavor text. Let me know what you think. is it going along the path that you were thinking of when you designed it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Sophros</span><br /> <br /> <i>Magic is the Wheel on which the world turns. The wheel turns bringing balance to the universe. Life and Death is balanced upon the wheel. The cycle continues to turn the wheel. We Awakened in Elysium, and drank from the Wooden Chalice.</i><br /> <br /> The Great Wheel can be seen everywhere and permeates existence itself. The very cosmos itself turns upon the wheels bringing life, death and rebirth to the stars. The Sophros are the caretakers of the wheel and insure that the balance is maintained. They have existed in one form or another since the dawn of man documenting the turning of the wheel. Since its infancy man\u2019s journey upon the wheel started and with each turn of the wheel man enters a new age. The ancient Greeks wrote about the ages of man starting with the Golden Age, the creation. It progresses through the Silver, Bronze and it will end with the Iron Age. These wide reaching views can be broken down further but they show the big picture.<br /> <br /> It could be said that everything is on an individual wheel, as each man starts his life thus starting his wheel. He starts in the spring of life progressing though his summer, autumn and finally his winter. However this is not and individual wheel is just represents his position on the great wheel. Looking at the wheel we know that the closer you get to the center of the wheel the faster the wheel turns giving the perception of an individual wheel. Stepping away from the wheel we see that what appeared as an individual wheel is contained within the section of mankind. The further we step out the more insignificant the things at the center appear.<br /> <br /> The Sophros know that man\u2019s time on the wheel will end giving birth to something new. We do not fear the end, we celebrate it, as it is proof that the wheel is turning. We are continually fighting the lie that we have a choice in how it turns, we do not. The path on the wheel is forever consistent with our position on the wheel. The ride will end when it is supposed to and nothing can stop that. Even those that claim immortality will face an end and then they do it will be seen that their path was only slightly further from the center than everyone else's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T04:54:06-08:00","id":1036541,"title":"","content":"With your permission, I'll copy this into the Sophros write-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T05:08:16-08:00","id":1036545,"title":"","content":"No need for my permission I am just adding flavor text. As I stated I started on this one because it is the one I identify with the most , if others picked one that interested them and did the fluff it would get done in no time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T05:16:38-08:00","id":1036549,"title":"","content":"BTW I truly feel that their Inferior Arcanum should be Fate. The way I see them fate is written on the wheel and is set. There is no altering it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:06:36-08:00","id":1036631,"title":"","content":"You're aware that Time is the Arcanum that deals with prophecies, right? Future inevitability is very much Time-related. Fate is more about probability manipulation and binding oaths than it is about predicting the future or defying a prediction. Fate is Inferior to the Aretoi because they tend to have little tolerance for chaos and chance; it clashes with their interest in precision and order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:13:40-08:00","id":1036637,"title":"","content":"Ok then time it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:15:51-08:00","id":1036640,"title":"","content":"Future is not set. It is stated in the entry to Time arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:24:06-08:00","id":1036645,"title":"","content":"Then <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> is correct. Time would be harder for them to manipulate because they do not believe that concept. The way I envision them, and have written them, they feel that everything is written on the wheel and is solid IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-23-2017, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T23:12:56-08:00","id":1037058,"title":"","content":"Possible solution to the Aretos Watchtower issue: follow in the footsteps of the M\u00e6stroi. That is, instead of &lt;material&gt; &lt;object&gt;, do &lt;material&gt; and &lt;material&gt;. So \u201cHermium and ___\u201d. Not sure what the second material should be; but I'd want something that isn't one of the Perfected Metals \u2014 hermium already covers that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T02:09:55-08:00","id":1037092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=883344#post883344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <hr /><i>Designer's Notes:</i> The Sophros are based on chthonic mythology (where I use the term in its original meaning, as opposed to the \u201cof the Underworld\u201d sense that <b>Mage</b> has been using): Persephone is a good touchstone to use. They deal in nurturing in the Spring and harvesting in the Fall, the cycle of life, death, and rebirth.<br /> <br /> I've never been able to get the imagery right for this. Yggdrasil not only works better as an Emanation, it <i>is</i> an Emanation (note that the Other Five are older than <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>). Perhaps \u201cEden\u201d would work better? I think a Supernal garden would be quite appropriate for this Path. As well, I've never been able to come up with Supernal Entities for this Realm that I'm happy with. Right now, I'm leanig toward Serpents (i.e., wyrms and snakes) and/or Ents (i.e., sapient trees).<br /> <br /> More to come.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">I am going to work this into the Sophros as the world tree, the branches connect to the heavens, the trunk connects to the Terrestrial and the roots to the underworld. However I can't find any realm the connects to the other realms. The world tree itself isn't a realm but in most cultures it connects the realms. Elysium is the Greek heaven, Hades is the Greek underworld and they are connected by the world (cosmic) tree. I like the Idea of a Supernal Garden and the Garden of Eden can fit that bill.<br /> <br /> As for Supernal Entities Serpents, Ents, and Dryads (from Greek Mythology) fit the bill.<br /> <br /> Yggdrasil is Norse and is the tree that connects all the realms above and below to the Terrestrial, but again it isn't a realm.<br /> <br /> Druid in particular is Celtic. The Opham tree is the World Tree and it all predates Christianity. There is alot of information on Opham so that would be easy to incorporate. But once again the tree just connects to the after realms and is not a realm in and of itself.<br /> <br /> I guess the question is, Which way do you want to go with this and do you want to stick with Elysium. I feel if we are going to continue down the Druid line we should go with the Celtic view but the choice is your as the original designer.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In the D&amp;D cosmology there is the Outlands that connects all other realms.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-24-2017, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T04:46:11-08:00","id":1037123,"title":"","content":"Researching this a little more the Ethereal realm touches all the other realms. But in Mage the Ethearial realm is twilight correct? So that wouldn't work either. Maybe I am overthinking this and Elysium will do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T20:26:21-07:00","id":1082500,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any idea for what the Serpents of Elysium would be? (Like how the Angels of the Aether are Seraphim and Cherubim) We have a Sophros in one of our games (Yes, we use these Paths in our games) and he wants to be a Summoner and we've been trying to get ideas for what sort of mythical serpents to use as denizens of Elysium, but we've been having trouble. Help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13269-particlestabilitybalance","name":"ParticleStabilityBalance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T20:44:00-07:00","id":1082505,"title":"","content":"Well, we could have Coatl, probably for Life (since Quetzalcoatl of Aztec myth was the twin of the canine death god Xolotl), but I'm not sure what would represent Death alongside it.<br /> <br /> Or we could use Dragons (Life) and Basilisks (Death).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T11:18:52-08:00","id":1180458,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the necro but I\u2019m thinking about incorporating it in my games<br /> <br /> For the tarot cards associated with the Path<br /> <br /> <b>Aretos</b>: <b>The Emperor </b>prince of the material world and <b>The Star </b>light of the night. The two cards are linked in a way. The Emperor is the stereotypical powerful man but the Star depicts an act of blessing an creation. One creates by taking and ordering and the other by giving and letting grow. Furthermore, the Star in the Awakened Tarot is Prime.<br /> <br /> <b>Axios: The Lover </b>is a given as the original design of the man between two women indicates choices and social situations. For the second <b>The Magician </b>could work. It\u2019s associated with Mercury and could work as the Fate card with an emphasis on the trickster-role. I would certainly not taken it for the Caelum version of the Path but it could work with the archetypes of merchants.<br /> <br /> <b>Kleos: The High Priestess </b>being taken by the Obrimo\u00ef is not really fitting IMHO and reeks of someone wanting to put the two religious figureheads on the Path. Both interpretation of the card, the intuition or the bookish knowledge can work for the bards. As for the Time, <b>Judgement</b> is both interpreted as something coming back from the past or a messenger. It could present a dilemma: Keep knowledge secret or disseminate it?<br /> <br /> <b>Maestros: The Tower </b>is actually apt for these guys. I mean they\u2019re the lightning and the fire and command to the elements. There is a reading of the Tower card where what breaks the edifice is not thunder from above but something escaping from within. <b>The Chariot </b>is a reminder that the power should not be mastering you but also depicts an act of taming appropriate for the path.<br /> <br /> <b>Sophros: The Empress </b>mother of nature is a given but I\u2019m wondering if <b>The Hanged Man</b> would be appropriate for the second card. The Hanged Man can be read as a period of rest and growth. When you get it in a reading the message is generally stay put. For druids attuned to the seasons it could be an interesting dilemma: Whether to force growth or decay or let it happen on its own.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T14:20:45-08:00","id":1180503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1180458#post1180458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the necro</div> </div> </div> </div> This is what I tend to call a \u201cproject thread\u201d, as opposed to a discussion thread. As I see it, that makes its status with regards to necro different from conversations that die out and oughtn't be resurrected: as long as you're contributing to the project, it doesn't matter how long it's been dormant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1180458#post1180458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I\u2019m thinking about incorporating it in my games<br /> <br /> For the tarot cards associated with the Path<br /> <br /> <b>Aretos</b>: <b>The Emperor </b>prince of the material world and <b>The Star </b>light of the night. The two cards are linked in a way. The Emperor is the stereotypical powerful man but the Star depicts an act of blessing an creation. One creates by taking and ordering and the other by giving and letting grow. Furthermore, the Star in the Awakened Tarot is Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1180458#post1180458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Axios: The Lover </b>is a given as the original design of the man between two women indicates choices and social situations. For the second <b>The Magician </b>could work. It\u2019s associated with Mercury and could work as the Fate card with an emphasis on the trickster-role. I would certainly not taken it for the Caelum version of the Path but it could work with the archetypes of merchants.</div> </div> </div> </div>and diplomats. And deal-makers in general. Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1180458#post1180458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Kleos: The High Priestess </b>being taken by the Obrimo\u00ef is not really fitting IMHO and reeks of someone wanting to put the two religious figureheads on the Path. Both interpretation of the card, the intuition or the bookish knowledge can work for the bards. As for the Time, <b>Judgement</b> is both interpreted as something coming back from the past or a messenger. It could present a dilemma: Keep knowledge secret or disseminate it?</div> </div> </div> </div> The only qualm I have with this is the notion that someone on the Path of Enlightenment might seriously consider keeping knowledge secret. Though, given that knowledge is power, and with great power comes great responsibility\u2026<br /> <br /> In general, though, I see the Kleos erring on the side of \u201cdisseminate it\u201d.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1180458#post1180458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Maestros: The Tower </b>is actually apt for these guys. I mean they\u2019re the lightning and the fire and command to the elements. There is a reading of the Tower card where what breaks the edifice is not thunder from above but something escaping from within. <b>The Chariot </b>is a reminder that the power should not be mastering you but also depicts an act of taming appropriate for the path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1180458#post1180458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sophros: The Empress </b>mother of nature is a given but I\u2019m wondering if <b>The Hanged Man</b> would be appropriate for the second card. The Hanged Man can be read as a period of rest and growth. When you get it in a reading the message is generally stay put. For druids attuned to the seasons it could be an interesting dilemma: Whether to force growth or decay or let it happen on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div> My knowledge of the tarot is minimal; so unless someone objects, I'm inclined to defer to your reasoning here. \u201cHanged Man\u201d also makes me think of something dying, which plays into the \u201caging and dying\u201d half of the cycle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T14:33:56-08:00","id":1180506,"title":"","content":"The Empress and the Hanged Man are already connected numerologically in Tarot symbolism, so pairing the two is natural. The Hanged Man also implies sacrifice, and I now have this image of watering the trees and the fields with blood...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T15:05:29-08:00","id":1180512,"title":"","content":"OK; I've taken ganonso's suggestions and have integrated them (mostly word for word) into the Path write-ups. In so doing, I also made a slight tweak to the Kleos, replacing \u201cstories\u201d with \u201cfables\u201d \u2014 a fable being a story intended to teach.<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking that the \u201cBeyond the ___\u201d sections should probably include one or two of the original Paths, too \u2014 specifically, ones where there's potential for confusion or overlap, and where some commentary might shed some light on what the distinctions are. For instance, sorcerers and theurges both tend to be rather\u2026 assertive types. A sorcerer's thoughts on the Obrimos could help clarify how the Obrimos and M\u00e6stros mindsets differ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T16:06:58-08:00","id":1180525,"title":"","content":"Other things that I need at this point: <br /> <br /> 1. to complete the Symbols and Myths sections, I need summaries of how each Path sees its Supernal Entities, and a sense of how their magic works/what they do with it.<br /> <br /> 2. \u201cThree ___s\u201d: this shouldn't be hard; three sample character concepts demonstrating how diverse the Path is.<br /> <br /> 3. ___s in the Orders: the Path as seen through the lens of each Order.<br /> <br /> 4. Building the ___\u2019s Mystery: character creation advice for the Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T21:58:19-08:00","id":1180608,"title":"","content":"The Watchtower of Brass and Flame is in the Realm of the Elemental Nation and inhabited by Elementals, including the djinn.<br /> <br /> I chose Elemental Nation using the Primal Wild as my inspiration: an adjective-noun pair. I chose Elemental because the Realm is composed of elemental forces: fire, lightning, heat, light, sound, etc. But those forces move with purpose, guided by alien intelligence; and the denizens are likewise composed of purposeful forces \u2014 it's a realm where everything is not just alive, not just sentient, but <i>sapient</i>. It's not all one mind, and the individual entities in this Realm are organized by hierarchies of mastery and service into something resembling civilization. Essentially everything in the Realm is part of a vast Nation, including the Realm itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T05:51:44-08:00","id":1180676,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s see how these Paths get to the Seers<br /> <br /> <b>Aretos </b>are even more suited to Mammon or Pantechnicon than Moros. They consider themselves as craftsman, using Matter and Prime to gird their brothers in the faith with magical armaments. For the Sleepers they would be concerned with potentials, not in the sense of Destinies (which with their Inferior Arcanum being Fate, most won\u2019t perceive) but mundanely. Those whose advances can help the Exarchs are showered with gifts while their enemies received cursed items enchanted to bear their doom.<br /> <br /> <b>Axios </b>are imbued with the power to see what\u2019s important to you and bind you with your own words. Faustian Pacts are the first image that comes to mind when describing Axios Seers. As Seers their pacts always drive the victim to a position where she cannot awaken. Sometimes that means they work and are caught in material riches, sometimes they are destroyed by the promises they have made. Also Fate will enable them to see who is important and who is not.<br /> <br /> <b>Kleos: </b>Nothing springs immediately to mind as this Path is the one I understand the less. 1984\u2019s style operatives who manage knowledge of the past and erase Atlanteans Ruins from the memory? Inquisitors who use their Arcanum as a means to decide guilt or innocence? (That\u2019s one is nice for the Guardians of the Veil though)? The theme of the Path seems to be knowledge so false teachers are a given but beyond that.<br /> <br /> <b>Maestros </b>are in command. Over their spirit-slaves, over the elements and the Sleepers. They are the warriors of the Seers using destructive magic at their leisure. Like the Aretos are actually better servants of the Chancellors, I would see the Maestros as the servants of the General and at such they will use spirits to incite violence and Forces to burn their foes. More subtly Forces means no modern technology can really stop you and few secrets in computers are secrets for you.<br /> <br /> <b>Sophros </b>are masters of growth and decay, two processes that makes them uniquely suited to cater to the mortal charges of the Seers. Not only rot and decay will bring fear to most people but controlling the food supply makes you lord over pretty much everyone. More largely they would be pretty terrifying as I see blood sacrifice and traditional Witchcraft being a big part of the Sophro\u00ef praxis.<br /> <br /> In other matters a tentative list of Aeons<br /> <br /> Aretos: Vulcanus (Matter), Venus Ourania (Prime)<br /> Axios: A trickster like Mercury or Coyote, perhaps seek in Asian mythology for kitsune<br /> Kleos: Thot? Prometheus? White Buffalo Woman? Culture heroes? <br /> Maestros: Al-Rayman (Spirit), a great super-intelligent bull, and Falak (Spirit), a great flaming serpent<br /> Sophros: Xipe Totec (Life), Santa Muerte (Death)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T09:04:09-08:00","id":1180738,"title":"","content":"For the Kleos, 1984-style \u201chistory is what we say it is\u201d is very appropriate. Kleos Seers are propagandists, subverting the education system to indoctrinate children to spread the Lie; they're the teachers who are more interested in students who blindly support the cause (whatever that may be) rather than students who think for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T10:23:26-08:00","id":1180791,"title":"","content":"Also: the M\u00e6stros Seers strike me as more likely to favor the Hegemony over the Praetorians: while their command of Forces lends itself nicely to violent pursuits, their defining feature is not violence; it's authority and duty. But where the Pentacle Sorcerers see a harmony between the two (e.g., the M\u00e6stros has a duty to serve those in his charge), their Seer counterparts see it as more of a one-way street.<br /> <br /> M\u00e6stros Seers are the guys who think they can run your life better than you can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-24-2018, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T07:09:58-08:00","id":1181118,"title":"","content":"So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> have you thought about the Mysteries that drive someone to awaken to these Paths? For the moment my idea are<br /> <br /> Aretos: Building something: Strange Artifacts to understand<br /> Axios: Mapping a place that shouldn't exist?<br /> Kleos: No idea<br /> Maestros: Summoning?<br /> Sophros; Sacrifice?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T14:10:24-08:00","id":1189286,"title":"","content":"I've been holding off on addressing the various Awakenings until I see what <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> does for the official Paths' Awakenings. Likewise with the various Paths' manifestations in the Lie. <br /> <br /> In other news, I've recently been reading the <b>Revised Verbena Tradition Book</b> for <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, and was struck by how many of those concepts resonate with the Sophros. Frankly, I think that the Sophros capture the essence of \u201cWitch\u201d far better than the Acanthus do, just as the Aretos capture the essence of \u201cAlchemist\u201d far better than the Moros. Not that I intend to change anything in this regard; the official Paths have claimed Witch and Alchemist, and so be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T09:27:27-08:00","id":1193168,"title":"","content":"I do not have it completed but this is what I have for the Sophros so far. Of course not everything listed below is my work. This was a community effort.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sophros<br /> The Druids<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Magic is the Wheel on which the world turns. The wheel turns bringing balance to the universe. Life and Death is balanced upon the wheel. The cycle continues to turn the wheel. We Awakened in Concordant Opposition, and drank from the Wooden Chalice. The Cosmic Tree (World Tree, Tree of Life, Yggdrasil, Opham Tree, The One Tree) sits at the center of the Wheel connecting to all the realms. The realm of Concordant Opposition is the Cosmic Tree and to get to the other realm one travels the branches and roots.</i><br /> <br /> The Great Wheel can be seen everywhere and permeates existence itself. The very cosmos turns upon the wheels bringing life, death and rebirth to the stars. The Sophros are the caretakers of the wheel and insure that the balance is maintained. They have existed in one form or another since the dawn of man documenting the turning of the wheel. Since its infancy man\u2019s journey upon the wheel started and with each turn of the wheel man enters a new age. The ancient Greeks wrote about the ages of man starting with the Golden Age, the creation. It progresses through the Silver, Bronze and it will end with the Iron Age. These wide reaching views can be broken down further but they show the big picture.<br /> It could be said that everything is on an individual wheel, as each man starts his life thus starting his wheel. He starts in the spring of life progressing though his summer, autumn and finally his winter. However this is not and individual wheel is just represents his position on the great wheel. Looking at the wheel we know that the closer you get to the center of the wheel the faster the wheel turns giving the perception of an individual wheel. Stepping away from the wheel we see that what appeared as an individual wheel is contained within the section of mankind. The further we step out the more insignificant the things at the center appear.<br /> The Sophros know that man\u2019s time on the wheel will end giving birth to something new. We do not fear the end, we celebrate it, as it is proof that the wheel is turning. We are continually fighting the lie that we have a choice in how it turns, we do not. The path on the wheel is forever consistent with our position on the wheel. The ride will end when it is supposed to and nothing can stop that. Even those that claim immortality will face an end and then they do it will be seen that their path was only slightly further from the center than everyone else\u2019s.<br /> <br /> <b>Sophros Awakenings</b><br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Sophros Magic</b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcana</b><br /> <b>Life and Death: </b>They are the basis of balance, representing the eternal wheel: Elysium energies<br /> <br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum</b><br /> <b>Time:</b> all things happen in their own time, and the Sophros must honor that. Thus, messing with the flow of time is hard for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols and Myths</b><br /> The Empress, mother of nature. The Hanged Man can be read as a period of rest and growth. When you get it in a reading the message is generally stay put. For druids attuned to the seasons it could be an interesting dilemma: Whether to force growth or decay or let it happen on its own.<br /> <br /> <b>Druidic Brews</b><br /> <b>Three Druids</b><br /> Brenden, an avid hiker, loves the majestic scenes of the mountains. I was on the mother of all hikes that his life changed. At the end of the Pacific Crest Trail after crossing the Bridge of the gods he mis-stepped and tumbled into the canyon below. At the bottom his mind slipped into darkness and his consciousness journeyed to Elysium. He awoke with the ability to heal his own body. His style of magic expounds on the feeling one gets from being outdoors. He is an adrenalin junky and enjoys stimulating that feeling in others. As a member of the Adamantine Arrow he now defends the nature he loves with the fierceness of nature itself.<br /> <br /> Adaline was awakened in collage as she studied to get her Doctorates of Internal medicine, her dream was to become a surgeon. With the powers of Life and Death at her disposal she has gained the acclaim that she always desired. As one of the few druids to take to being a Free Council she marries science, technology and magic to make the world around her a better place. Closely watched by the Guardians she holds the line not to be crossed even though she knew she could have saved the ones that she let slip into death. But even at that she was able to help guide the soul and make the most out of death.<br /> <br /> Jose is more interested in challenges one faces after death then what had happened before. Although he doesn\u2019t just study the death of a body, he feels that everything essentially experiences death. When a building erodes and falls to the ravages of time, is that not a death in and unto itself. With this in mind he studies decay of material was fervently as he studies the death of a body. As an archeologist he has had the pleasure of studying the remains of a dead culture, he has wiped away the decay and witnessed the beauty of the original piece, if only for a moment before the spell allows it to return to its new and equally beautiful state/ And yes he never misses D\u00eda de Muertos.<br /> <br /> <b>Druids in the Orders</b><br /> <b>The Adamantine Arrow:</b> These druids go by several name, Eco terrorist, Militant Druids, Tree huggers, whatever name you want to call them they are the protectors of the natural world. There are several organization that have sprung up in support of these druids namely green peace and PITA.<br /> <b>The Free Council:</b> There are very few Druids in the Fee Council, given that technology doesn\u2019t play much of a role in Life and Death. Those that do join the free council usually do so to manipulate the media and utilize the internet to further their cause. They also find that technology is a great way to hide their Life and Death magic as most things can be explained away as a technological miracle.<br /> <b>The Guardians of the Veil:</b> Life and Death are extremely suited to the views of the Guardians. Life is uniquely suited to the covert surveillance that the guardians are famous for. The use of the Death Arcamun as punishment for committing treasonous acts only strengthens their fear factor.<br /> <b>The Mysterium:</b> The Druids hold a solid footing amongst the Mystagogues Sages. Not only for their knowledge of Life and Death but for their relentless tracking of historic events. They have cut a place for their beliefs into every culture and civilization. They have played the role of Tribal Shaman, Village Healer, Wise Hermit and modern Doctors. The Wise Sages are been sought out for all sorts of matters and are generally looked at as the holders of the secrets of life and Death. That is because they are.<br /> <b>The Silver Ladder:</b> There Druids of modern time have lost some of the foothold that they had with the th\u00e9arch. Once they were considered the Wises around and therefore natural judges, however they have stepped back from that role and stepped further into their studies. A druid that has found himself a place within the ladder still lends his wisdom to the enlightenment of all mankind.<br /> <b>Seers of the Throne:</b> are masters of growth and decay, two processes that makes them uniquely suited to cater to the mortal charges of the Seers. Not only rot and decay will bring fear to most people but controlling the food supply makes you lord over pretty much everyone. More largely they would be pretty terrifying as I see blood sacrifice and traditional Witchcraft being a big part of the Sophro\u00ef praxis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Building a Druid's Mystery</b><br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Druidic Legacies</b><br /> <b>Existing Legacies:</b> <br /> Orphans of Proteus, Walkers in the Mists, Sodality of the Tor, Dreamspeakers, Tamers of Rivers, Thread Cutters, Tamers of Blood?<br /> <b>New Legacies:</b> Tamers of Trees?, The Hive? <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sophros: Druids</b> and <b>Blighters </b>on the Path to Elysium, Supernal Realm of Life and Death, and abode of Mythical Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T09:59:00-08:00","id":1193184,"title":"","content":"One nitpick: the Free Council isn't the \u201ctechnology order\u201d; it's the \u201chumanity is magical\u201d order, drawing symbols from human innovation. The Dreamspeakers are a Free Council Legacy. <br /> <br /> Another thought: the Cosmic Tree works beautifully as the Sophros Watchtower; there may not be need for a \u201cWatchtower of the Wooden Chalice\u201d. The Realm is still Elysium, a garden-like afterlife (with the \u201cgarden\u201d part representing Life and the \u201cafterlife\u201d part representing Death) inhabited by serpents (alternately guides and tempters) and saints (or something to that effect: ghost-like entities of a somewhat heavenly nature: the \u201cworthy dead\u201d who have earned a place in Elysium). That said, I can see Elysium being described as the \u201chub of the Great Wheel\u201d.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's the Abode of Heroes and Beasts? (Not to be confused with the Heroes and Beasts of <b>Beast: the Primordial</b>, any more than the Supernal Fae of the Acanthus are to be confused with the Gentry of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-08-2018, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:11:58-08:00","id":1193188,"title":"","content":"Ok I can work on the Free Council section a little more.<br /> <br /> I would agree that the Cosmic tree is a great Watchtower for the Sophros. And I like the Elysium as the Hub of the Great Wheel. I didn't think of the Garden part of it and I can see where that all fits together. I will add the Garden part to the write-up.<br /> <br /> I have limited time to work on this type of stuff but I hope to finish the Sophros soon. Is there another one that you want me to try to take on next once I am done with the current part?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:21:58-08:00","id":1193191,"title":"","content":"Whichever one interests you the most. This is supposed to be a labor of love, after all. That said, the Axios are probably the most in need of work, considering their drastic reimagining from the original concept (astrologers and explorers) to their current concept (traders and advocates). A lot of their write-up right now is a holdover from the original concept, and needs to be replaced with something more suitable to the new concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T12:20:43-08:00","id":1193247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1193188#post1193188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I can work on the Free Council section a little more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technology vs innovation doesn't seem like it would make a lot of difference to their level of involvement with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T18:22:45-08:00","id":1193382,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> The write ups for the original Paths don\u2019t have any language in them to encourage or discourage membership in any of the Orders. I\u2019d take a cue from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T02:14:53-08:00","id":1193470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1193247#post1193247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technology vs innovation doesn't seem like it would make a lot of difference to their level of involvement with it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not sure I get where you are going with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1193382#post1193382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> The write ups for the original Paths don\u2019t have any language in them to encourage or discourage membership in any of the Orders. I\u2019d take a cue from that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wasn't implying that they had any particular difficulty with any Order, just that they prefer one Order over the other. Those that have embraced the less preferred Orders still find a place amongst their members. This is true with almost any path the path itself doesn't encourage or discourage, it is just tendencies of the the path to prefer one over the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T02:40:44-08:00","id":1193473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></di