 not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-18T16:51:20-08:00","id":1497493,"title":"","content":"Aretos Need more work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T00:55:03-07:00","id":1512095,"title":"","content":"The just-released Tome of the Pentacle is right up the alley of the Kleos in many ways, given their interest in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T01:42:15-07:00","id":1512102,"title":"","content":"Aside from the fae and demons (which have already been used by the Acanthus and Mastigos), what kinds of mythological creatures are known for establishing pacts? I'm trying to think of a Supernal Entity for the Axios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T02:33:32-07:00","id":1512104,"title":"","content":"Dragons, maybe? If you're willing to loosely interpret &quot;pacts&quot; as &quot;accept tribute and/or declare a place their hoard&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T03:59:06-07:00","id":1512201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1512102#post1512102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the fae and demons (which have already been used by the Acanthus and Mastigos), what kinds of mythological creatures are known for establishing pacts? I'm trying to think of a Supernal Entity for the Axios.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>was</i> gonna suggest Deep Ones since their thing is trading underwater gold, treasures, and other valuables from the depths to coastal communities in exchange for holding influence and sway in said communities, acquiring new followers for Dagon, establishing blood ties, the whole 'that which gives life also takes' vibe of the sea etc. but I'm not sure they have enough precedent as <i>mythological</i> creatures rather than simply fictional ones, even if I feel they fit the watery vibe of the Axios. Otherwise, consider sirens, nereids and oceanids, dragons etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T11:38:39-07:00","id":1512228,"title":"","content":"Ideas for the Kleos Roles <b>in the Orders</b>\u200b?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","user":"Phoenix853457","date":". 05-23-2023, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T15:37:46-07:00","id":1512310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1512102#post1512102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the fae and demons (which have already been used by the Acanthus and Mastigos), what kinds of mythological creatures are known for establishing pacts? I'm trying to think of a Supernal Entity for the Axios.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an Unorthodox idea: what if the Axios summon... Mages?<br /> meaning the Supernal Beings of their Path are based on wizards, the same way the original five Paths summon beings inspired by angels,demons,fae,spirits and ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T16:08:40-07:00","id":1512313,"title":"","content":"Setting aside for the moment the issue that mages are directly related to the Supernal already (unlike angels, demons, fae, spirits, and ghosts), what would a Supernal Entity based on them bring to the table that's particularly suitable to the Axios?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T18:11:06-07:00","id":1512319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1512313#post1512313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside for the moment the issue that mages are directly related to the Supernal already (unlike angels, demons, fae, spirits, and ghosts), what would a Supernal Entity based on them bring to the table that's particularly suitable to the Axios?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly the idea is that the Axios are all about trading,give or take,the law of equivalent exchange right? that all seems very common in wizards as character tropes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T05:45:43-07:00","id":1512434,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea for Axios supernal entities. Kings (space) and Beggars (fate).<br /> <br /> Kings are space because they're linked to their kingdoms, when found in Terra Incognita they usually symbolically rule it. The challenges they set usually involve travel, quest and fetch me X. My friend, come sail the dangerous seas to celebrate my triumphs, there will be gifts for all.<br /> <br /> Beggars are fate, when you meet a beggar you have all the power, you can give wealth, you can walk away, you can bully them. There will be no consequences. Except, what you do shows who you are and who you are creates your fate. Their tests are usually moral dilemmas.<br /> <br /> Plus. The phrase &quot;kings and beggars&quot; feels like it could come straight from Arabian Nights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T07:23:26-07:00","id":1512452,"title":"","content":"have Ideas for the Axios Roles <b>in the Orders</b>\u200b?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T08:49:52-07:00","id":1512743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix853457</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e?p=1512452#post1512452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">have Ideas for the Axios Roles <b>in the Orders</b>\u200b?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><b>free council:</b> loretraders , trading with other orders about artifacts and grimoires , maybe also serving as third party middleman between such trades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T10:56:33-07:00","id":1512748,"title":"","content":"Basically, cultural exchange. Since the <i>Free Council</i> is about finding the Supernal in humanity, the lore that they trade wouldn't just be artifacts and grimoires (which would actually be more Mysterium than Free Council); it would also be the sorts of things that Free Council Techn\u00ea are made of. Remember, the Axios are diplomats as well as traders: they're as much about bringing communities together as they are about making money. So stuff about understanding belief systems is very much in their wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> For the <i>Adamantine Arrow</i>, everything is conflict; so the Axios in their ranks apply that to deal-making. These are your born hagglers.<br /> <br /> The <i>Guardians of the Veil</i>'s Axios focus on the seedier side of deal-making: the best of them are the ones who facilitate the deals that are necessary but that nobody wants to admit to, while the worst of them run criminal cartels.<br /> <br /> As mentioned above, the <i>Mysterium</i> is where you'll find Axios trading artifacts and grimoires.\u200b<br /> <br /> Where the Free Council Axios are about cultural exchange, the <i>Silver Ladder</i> Axios are about political exchange: about as purely diplomatic as you're ever likely to find.<br /> <br /> The Axios of the <i>Seers of the Throne</i> are about as close to Ascension's Syndicate as you can get, focusing on corporate power as a tool of social control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-25-2023, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T08:15:41-07:00","id":1513533,"title":"","content":"have Ideas for the Kleos Roles <b>in the Orders</b>\u200b?\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T08:58:16-07:00","id":1513536,"title":"","content":"Tell you what: why don't you post <i>your </i>ideas? As it stands, your participation in this thread thus far has been nothing but a series of requests or demands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span><